'''San Chorche''' ({{Langx|an|{{W|Saint George}}}}; {{Langx|kp|Honuokã|4=place of canoes}}) is a city within the [[Camaca|Kamakã]] [[regions of Balisca|region]] of the [[Bayara|Bayaran community]]. It is located in the northern extremity of the region, straddling the border between Kamakã and [[Carpinchera]]. As of the [[2025 Baliscan census]], it had a population of slightly under 1.5 million people, making it the fourth-most populous city in Bayara, and the eighth-most populous in [[Balisca]]. 

